WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:10.600
The Great Wall of China was funded by a state
lottery.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:16.230
Sylvester Stallone was so broke before his
script for Rocky was accepted that he sold

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.020
his dog for $25.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:22.790
A few weeks later, he bought it back for $15,000.

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:31.480
In 2012, 146 girls in the US were named Khaleesi.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:37.750
The first person to smoke in Europe was sent
to prison for being possessed by the devil.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:43.090
India's Mars probe cost less than the movie
Gravity.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:45.680
Fruits are the ovaries of plants.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:53.420
In 1859, a panic swept America because young
people were playing too much chess.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.160
The longest bout of hiccups lasted 67 years.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.710
Elephants tickle each other.

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:06.259
Apple is worth more than Sweden, Poland and
Nigeria.

00:01:06.259 --> 00:01:10.670
At 21, Mussolini was homeless and living under
a bridge in Switzerland.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:18.350
At the 1956 Olympics, Russian rower Vyacheslav
Ivanov was so excited at winning gold that

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:23.119
he dropped his medal into the lake and it
was never found.

00:01:23.119 --> 00:01:29.469
Before having their chests cut open and their
hearts pulled out, Aztec human-sacrifice victims

00:01:29.469 --> 00:01:31.969
were given a cup of hot chocolate.

00:01:31.969 --> 00:01:37.340
Prince Charles runs his Aston Martin on biofuel
made from wine.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:41.209
All glossy magazines are radioactive.

00:01:41.209 --> 00:01:47.090
Azodicarbonamide is a chemical compound that
makes things softer and bouncier.

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:55.700
It's used in flip-flops, yoga mats and McDonald's
Big Mac buns.

